    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d343">

                <pb facs="0350" n="1028" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1028"/>

                <head>Mr. Pruyn to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Yedo</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-06-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 9, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Agreeably to your instructions contained in
                    despatch No. 7, of the 5th of February, I addressed to Lieutenant Colonel E. St.
                    John Neale, her Britannic Majesty’s charge d’affaires and consul general during
                    the absence of Mr. Alcock, a letter, of which enclosure No. 1 is a copy, and
                    also transmit No. 2, copy of his reply.</p>
                <p>I have as yet received no reply to a letter addressed by me to the minister of
                    foreign affairs on the same subject.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister
                        Resident.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d343-a1.xml" xpointer="d343-a1"/>
